  m_Name: Scene10_FAQ_2
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::OhmsLaw.DialogueLine
  id: Scene10_FAQ_2
  speaker: WATTSON
  text: The potential difference is the push on the charges in the wire. A bigger
    push makes the free electrons drift along faster, so more charge crosses each
    section of the wire every second, and that is a bigger current. Look at your
    table to see exactly how much bigger.
